Vendored third-party assets
---------------------------

The offline HTML report inlines the following MIT-licensed JavaScript libraries.
They are shipped as part of the installed wheel and are not fetched at runtime.
Versions, SHA-256 digests and upstream URLs are recorded in
src/nhi_blast/report/assets/MANIFEST.json.

  Cytoscape.js 3.30.4
  Copyright (c) 2016-2024, The Cytoscape Consortium.
  https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js
  License: MIT (full text retained in the vendored file header)

  dagre 0.8.5
  https://github.com/dagrejs/dagre
  License: MIT

  cytoscape-dagre 2.5.0
  https://github.com/cytoscape/cytoscape.js-dagre
  License: MIT

The offline HTML report also embeds two WOFF2 font subsets as data URIs. They are
shipped in the installed wheel, are not fetched at runtime, and are recorded with
digests in src/nhi_blast/report/assets/MANIFEST.json.

  Geist (latin subset)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio
  https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (full text in
  src/nhi_blast/report/assets/fonts/OFL.txt)

  Geist Mono (latin subset)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio
  https://github.com/vercel/geist-font
  License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (full text in
  src/nhi_blast/report/assets/fonts/OFL.txt)

Platform data
-------------

The files under src/nhi_blast/data/ describe GitHub Actions and AWS IAM
behaviour. Each file records its primary source URL and the date on which it was
verified; see docs/data-provenance.md. Those documents remain the property of
their respective publishers and are not redistributed here. The data files are
this project's own summaries, not copies of vendor documentation.

Runtime dependencies (installed separately, not vendored)
---------------------------------------------------------

pydantic, PyYAML, networkx, typer, click and their transitive dependencies are
distributed under their own licences. Optional extras add rich (MIT) and
python-hcl2 with lark and regex (MIT). None of these packages is bundled in the
NHI-Blast wheel or sdist.
